# The Silence of Candlekeep

## Scene summary (from gm-assist, verbatim)

*Standing over a healed Tadric, the party notices an ominous change in the atmosphere of the keep as the eternal prophecies suddenly fall silent.*

- The party stands over a healed Tadric, having just rescued him from Moziqodo.
- Grygum notices that the endless chant of prophecies — a constant sound throughout Candlekeep — has suddenly and unnervingly stopped. He asks if this was ever mentioned before; the DM clarifies it's a continuous reading of prophecies that get deleted when fulfilled.
- Tadric notices that Moziqodo is dead and urges that they must tell Sylvira.
- The party deflects — Grygum suggests someone who knows Sylvira should do it, Daz says "We'll take care of it later" — and prioritizes heading to the High Tower to stop A'lai Aivenmore.
- Tadric insists on accompanying the party: "I faced Moziqodo! I faced the full… I… no, I, I, I will…" — he's "suffering from a desperate desire to be heroic."
- Grygum offers reassurance: "I do have resurrection magic if worst comes to worst."

## Verbatim moments

**[GM]**
- The party stands over a healed Tadric.

**[GM]**
> "Just as you're standing there, the acoustics deliver a sound from far off in the key. The endless chant has stopped. Now, one of the most important things about Candlekeep, just so you guys know, is that there's this endless chant of the prophecies."

**[Grygum]**
> "Was this ever mentioned? I don't remember this."

**[Daz]**
> "I mentioned on the first day that we were there, maybe. Yeah, yeah."

**[GM]**
> "They continuously read the prophecies, and every time a prophecy comes true. They delete the prophecy and keep repeating, right?"

**[Grygum]**
> "So, if Grygum is anything like me, then, I haven't noticed it for, like, the last 3 days anyway. Once it stops, I notice that it stopped."

**[GM]**
> "Yes, but you also notice it because Tadric is kind of like… stunned. Like, this is, like, this never happens."

**[GM — Tadric]**
> "Sylvira Savikas… someone needs to tell Sylvira Savikas that her son is dead."

**[Grygum]**
> "Oh, well, Ugh."

**[Grygum]**
> "It might best be someone who knows Sylvira Savikas."

**[Daz]**
> "We'll take care of it later."

**[GM]**
> "It's a later kind of problem, right?"

**[Daz]**
> "Yeah, it's a later… it's a later… Emerald the Ember Vanguard, or whatever we're calling ourselves these days."

**[GM — Tadric]**
> "I held it all night, and I didn't know what it was. Now that I know what it is, I'm not giving it to you and going to bed."

**[Tadric insisting on accompanying the party]**
> "I faced… I faced Moziqodo! I faced the full… I… no, I, I, I will… he's… he's definitely suffering from a desperate desire to be heroic."

**[Grygum]**
> "Well, come along. I do have, resurrection magic if worst comes to worst."

**[GM — Tadric]**
> "If Daral Yashenti was here, he says, but, but what about me?"

**[Grygum]**
> "Well, I didn't have it then."
